Delivery Robot — Requirements
|Requirement ID|Description                                                                                                                                                                                            |Priority|
|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------|
|R-01          |The robot shall remain in the IDLE state, performing no navigation or delivery activity, until a delivery request is received.                                                                         |High    |
|R-02          |Upon receiving a delivery request while IDLE, the robot shall transition to the NAVIGATING state and begin moving toward the destination.                                                              |High    |
|R-03          |While in the NAVIGATING state, the robot shall continuously scan its surroundings for obstacles.                                                                                                       |High    |
|R-04          |If an obstacle is detected while NAVIGATING, the robot shall suspend normal navigation and transition to the AVOIDING_OBSTACLE state.                                                                  |High    |
|R-05          |Once an obstacle has been successfully avoided, the robot shall transition back to the NAVIGATING state and resume movement toward the destination.                                                    |High    |
|R-06          |The robot shall transition to the DELIVERING state only when it is in the NAVIGATING state and has reached the destination; it shall not enter DELIVERING directly from IDLE or from AVOIDING_OBSTACLE.|Critical|
|R-07          |After the package has been successfully delivered, the robot shall transition from DELIVERING to the RETURNING state and head back to the warehouse.                                                   |High    |
|R-08          |While NAVIGATING (including toward the destination or back to the warehouse), the robot shall continuously monitor its battery level.                                                                  |Medium  |
|R-09          |If the battery becomes critically low while NAVIGATING or AVOIDING_OBSTACLE, the robot shall abort the current delivery journey and transition to the RETURNING state.                                 |Critical|
|R-10          |Upon reaching the warehouse while in the RETURNING state, the robot shall transition to the IDLE state and become available for a new delivery request.                                                |High    |
